    "notes": "Swept smoothWindowSec x {0.015,0.03,0.05} and minProminenceDb x {2,3,4,5,6,8,10,14} (24 combos) against per-syllable tone classification accuracy on 1027 real double-syllable clips (both syllables citation-tone-clear, sandhi not applied -- a constant bias across all combos). NO combo meaningfully beats always-even-split (54.1%); best is +0.6pp at 36.7% peaks-rate. Most combos are WORSE than baseline. Conclusion: intensity-peak-based segmentation (de Jong & Wempe style, as implemented) does not reliably find genuine syllable boundaries on this corpus -- even when it reports method=peaks (structural success), the resulting boundaries are not meaningfully better than blindly splitting the clip in half. This is a real negative result, not a tuning gap: the threshold space was swept broadly and none of it clears the bar."
